{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785012137,"nonce":"bte99uggI4C77pVN2WNYC/+sm+M=","message":"Implemented on integrate/open-issues-2026-07-26 (ed1440e, 8fe9588, bcd1ee2).\n\nGET /v1/connections/{id}/preflight (Administer, like the rest of the surface) returns status ok|degraded|unknown plus required[], missing[], granted_permissions[], subscribed_events[]. Each entry carries a severity and a \"what silently breaks\" sentence. The required set lives in one place — crates/scarab-forge/src/preflight.rs, static tables keyed by ForgeKind with the pure missing()/is_degraded() diff (level ladder; an unknown level fails closed). The actual half is a new ForgePort::describe_capabilities (default Unsupported), implemented for GitHub over GET /app with the App JWT.\n\nDesign point worth recording: it answers 200 with status \"unknown\" rather than an error when the forge cannot be introspected or the credential does not resolve. \"Could not look\" must not render as healthy — that is the same silent-success failure this ticket is about. UI surfaces it as an AppPreflight line directly under the credential health line in Connections.tsx.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [x] endpoint reports missing events/permissions per GitHub connection\n- [x] Settings surfaces it next to the credential health line\n- [x] fake-forge tests for BOTH failure shapes (no events subscribed -\u003e names push/pull_request; no statuses grant -\u003e names statuses: write), plus healthy, un-introspectable, missing-credential, Viewer 403, unknown-connection 404\n- [x] no credential material in the payload (asserted)\n\nWorkspace suite 656/656 green; UI vitest 72/72; UI build clean.\n\nKNOWN GAP, deliberately not closed over: never exercised against a real GitHub App. describe_capabilities parses a real GET /app body in unit tests, but no live call was made — the failure mode is not reproducible offline and not k8s-observable. Forgejo has no introspection API, so its preflight always answers unknown; its requirement table is documentation-only.","files":null}]}